job_description:
Cyber Security Analyst

• Degree and 11+ years of experience; 4 additional years of relevant technical experience may be considered in lieu of degree;

• Network engineering and/or network security background;

• Experience with data aggregation and analysis tools (e.g., Splunk, Kibana);

• Basic knowledge of AI capabilities and applications for data analytics;

• Experience using Python;

• Chantilly, no core hours but schedule must be reasonable

Technical Targeting Analyst, UID4

• Bachelor’s Degree in a relevant technical field, or 4 additional years of relevant technical experience may be accepted in lieu of degree;

• 6+ years of experience across technical competencies, such as: analysis, network engineering, network security, vulnerability assessment, technical collection, penetration testing, red teaming, hardware engineering, software reverse engineering, cyber operations, and/or computer exploitation;

• 3+ cumulative years of experience across multiple INTs;

• Proven cyber and technical targeting background, and use of specific tools and databases to achieve technical objectives;

• Experience drafting specific types of intelligence reports and coordinating analyses across organizations;

• Experience analyzing current and emerging intelligence issues;

• Solid organizational skills and the willingness and ability to adapt to dynamic and unexpected customer requirements

• Desire: 11+ years of experience across technical competencies (analysis; network engineering; network security; vulnerability assessment; technical collection; penetration testing; red teaming). 7+ cumulative years with experience across multiple INTs; demonstrated knowledge

of microelectronics and semiconductors; foreign language proficiency in speaking, reading and/or listening.

General TTA,• Degree and 11+ years of experience; 4 additional years of relevant technical experience

Information Technology / Telecommunications Sr Security Compliance Analyst (hybrid)
• Miami, Florida
• Direct Hire

Job
• **** 13702

Work
• **** Hybrid
• *
• Availability to work at the Client’s site in Miami, FL (required);
• Experience in Information Technology and Information Security/Compliance, focusing on executing compliance frameworks and programs (e.g., PCI-DSS, SOX, HIPAA) (5+ years);
• Information/Cybersecurity and Compliance experience meeting IT GCs (5+ years);
• Experience with technology project management, including building processes, controls, operating procedures, and guidelines (5+ years);
• Audit experience;
• Evidence and Testing experience;
• Bachelor’s degree in computer science, IT compliance, audit, or a related area.
• Experience with One Trust;
• Experience with Risk Assessments or Risk frameworks;
• CISM or CISSP certifications;
• Training in Project Management, Product Management, or Agile approach;
• Master’s degree.
• Ensure IT practices adhere to relevant laws, regulations, and industry standards (e.g., SOX, PCI);
• Facilitate compliance of applications and infrastructure;
• Conduct assessments and implement controls to mitigate risks related to regulatory requirements;
• Monitor ongoing compliance activities, track regulatory changes, and prepare reports;
• Conduct internal assessments and reviews to evaluate the effectiveness of controls and identify areas for improvement;
• Assess the compliance of vendors and third-party service providers;
• Review and provide input to update IT policies, procedures, and standards to address compliance requirements.

Why apply?
• Work with one of the largest global vacation and cruise providers and a recognizable brand;
• Be a part of a diverse multicultural team and thrive in a fun and inclusive work environment dedicated to providing memorable and affordable vacations;
• Work with the leader in cutting-edge technology and programming;
• Be certain in your future as our Client is a stable and growing company with increasing revenue;
• Receive plenty of coaching and support from the team and current Vitaver consultants.

Enjoy a comprehensive employee benefits *
• Get paid on a bi-weekly basis;
• During the 1st year of employment – prorated amount of PTO and Sick Time. After – 14 days of PTO annually and 10 days of sick time annually;
• Eight paid holidays annually;
• Available health, dental, and vision plans;
• Flexible spending account;
• 401K retirement savings plan;
• Employee Stock Purchase plan;
• Short and long-term disability plan;
• Cruise benefits;
• Discount and complimentary memberships (various complimentary memberships, discount cards, and *
• ** theme parks, various restaurants, wholesale clubs, car rental agencies, and cell phone providers to name a few).

If this job is not for you, earn a $2,100.00 referral bonus in cash by referring a Candidate.

Vitaver & Associates, Inc. dba Vitaver Staffing
